  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\nWire Contour has its own start field, `WireContourOp.start` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/wire_edm.rs:61-63`): the start hole or threading point, world XY mm. A closed profile without it is refused at generation (`crates/app/src/operation/wire_verify.rs:57`). This field is separate from the shared start point. Wire Contour has no exit point.\n\n## Expected\n\n- The threading point is the start pick of the shared mechanism of #3324. A saved file with the old `start` key opens with the same value (question 2 of #3324).\n- Start: the cut begins at the threading point and enters the profile with its lead.\n- Exit: on an open run, the cut ends at the end nearest the exit pick. On a closed profile, the exit pick sets where the cut leaves, before the tab or the cut-off.\n- The 4-axis sync pair rule holds (`wire_edm.rs:110-112`).\n\nSeams: `crates/app/src/operation/wire_op.rs:334`, `wire_verify.rs:57,95,125`.\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- A closed profile without a threading point stays refused.\n- The threading point is outside the part material that stays (inside the slug, or in the start hole).\n- The lead from the threading point does not cross the profile.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A load test opens a file with the old `start` key and gets the same path, byte-identical.\n- A pin test shows an exit at the pick on an open run, and one shows an impossible pick refused by name.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous path. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped wire golden is byte-identical.\n\nSafety floor: this changes toolpaths and posted G-code.\n",
